1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,750
Why does every team want a left-handed pitcher?

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:07,100
For starters, most hitters grow up seeing far more right-handed pitching.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,600
A lefty's release angle and pitch movement can look completely different.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Then there's the lefty-on-lefty matchup.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:20,300
Left-handed hitters generally have a tougher time against pitchers throwing from the same side.

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,200
But here's another advantage: controlling runners.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:30,100
A left-handed pitcher naturally faces first base when delivering from the stretch, making it easier to watch the runner and threaten a pickoff.

8
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:36,900
And when you combine that with great stuff and command, you get a pitcher who can change an entire matchup.

9
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,800
That's why a quality lefty is such a valuable weapon.

